## Architecture (mirrors the accepted CommandHistoryPage gold-standard)
  - @MainActor @Observable StateMachineDebuggerPageModel consumes an injectable
    `StateMachineDataSource` seam whose four methods are the web hooks ported BY NAME —
    useVehicleStateMachine / useFSMStats / useFSMTransitions / useSignalSnapshot (ADR-004; the
    view holds no networking). SampleStateMachineDataSource is the preview/standalone default.
  - All chrome via P2 design tokens (Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius) and P3 shared
    components (TSGlassPanel, TSChartContainer, TSPieChart, TSBarChart, TSStatCard, TSDataTable,
    TSEmptyState, TSErrorDisplay, TSPagination, TSVehicleSelect, TSSelect, TSHelpTooltip, TSKVList,
    TSPanelTitle, TSCaption, TSStatGridSkeleton, TSTableSkeleton, TSChartSkeleton). Native Swift
    Charts only — never a WKWebView (ADR-005).
  - Adaptive macOS (regular) / iPhone (compact) via horizontalSizeClass (ADR-002/006).
  - Live state: the vehicle-state hero surfaces a >2-min staleness flag from `liveUpdatedAt`
    (model.isLiveStale → TSBadge "fsm.stale") per ADR-013.
  - The 4 data sources flow through the model's typed state (DebuggerState) + currentState/stats/
    snapshot slices; every literal resolves from Localizable.xcstrings (ADR-014), web key names kept.
  - Control-plane FSM data is unit-agnostic; SI converters (P1/S5) are not involved on this surface
    (the only physical readout, the snapshot inspector, renders the source's pre-formatted strings).

